  "summary": "mcp-remote OS command injection via malicious authorization_endpoint (CVE-2025-6514)",
  "details": "JFrog reported that mcp-remote 0.0.5 through 0.1.15 mishandles the authorization_endpoint URL received during OAuth init, so a malicious MCP server can trigger OS command execution on the client (full parameter control on Windows, limited on macOS/Linux). CVSS 9.6. Fixed in 0.1.16.",
